# Upstream Taskwarrior tests that fail on this fork, with calendar=gregorian
# and dayname.style=english, and why.  None of them is caused by the calendar:
# they come from PersianTask's other defaults, which upstream-tests.sh leaves
# as they are.  Pristine upstream passes all of them in the same environment.
#
# One test per line: its name, then the reason.  A reason starting with
# 'flaky' marks a test that fails only sometimes, which may pass or fail.

calendar.test.py   weekstart defaults to saturday, so the calendar's week starts on Sa; passes with weekstart=sunday
uda.test.py        the estimate and rcalendar UDAs are defined by default, so 'udas' lists 3 UDAs, not 1
version.test.py    the version is 3.5.0-persiantask.1, where the test expects upstream's 3.5.0
view_test.cpp      flaky: aborts now and then under heavy parallel load, in pristine upstream too
